  {
    "url": "/content/assets/17Sm3GIK3eWR6vwd3LFowGvPbeEwH4Bki",
    "name": "collage-4.jpg",
    "width": 1864,
    "height": 2446,
    "title": "Beauty Standards - Marilyn Monroe",
    "size": 1,
    "medium": "Collage [Beauty Magazines]",
    "dimensions": "12 x 18 in",
    "start_date": "2021",
    "end_date": "2021",
    "description": "Our exaggerated and ever-present expectations of self-appearance and beauty cause anxiety and mental illness. Marilyn Monroe set such expectations but also suffered from their consequences.  The collage shows Monroe’s face in eerie kaleidoscopic colors. The sensual lips and raised attentive eyebrows identify her humanity. The glaring eyes appear terrified and simultaneously terrifying. The eyes judge and respond to being judged. The collage is made out of snippets from old beauty magazines and points to the commercial motivation of the beauty industry to prey on people’s insecurities. Marilyn Monroe suffered from mental illness and substance abuse. Psychiatrists believe her borderline personality disorder was likely related to childhood trauma. Being objectified by America did not help. I like to believe, Monroe would today be a card-carrying feminist. Instead, she committed suicide at 36."
  },
